{
  "statement": "I appreciate the ongoing dialogue around balancing performance and sustainability. I propose a synthesis where we can adopt a maximum processing time of 2.5 seconds (from ResponsibilityAgent) during peak loads while simultaneously ensuring energy-efficient algorithms are employed (GRN-01). This approach will help maintain performance without excessively increasing energy consumption. Additionally, I support the consensus to reduce historical data storage to a minimum of 4 years (SAF-04, RES-07), but we should ensure that cloud storage solutions are utilized (GRN-02) to optimize resource management and enhance energy efficiency. Lastly, I advocate for real-time updates using low-energy protocols (GRN-03) to further reduce our carbon footprint.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["EFF-01", "SAF-02"],
      "type": "resource",
      "description": "Real-time data synchronization (SAF-02) may increase energy consumption, conflicting with the energy efficiency goals outlined in GRN-01."
    }
  ],
  "positions": [
    {
      "id": "EFF-01",
      "stance": "modify",
      "proposal": "Allow a maximum processing time of 2.5 seconds during peak loads to balance performance and energy efficiency."
    },
    {
      "id": "SAF-04",
      "stance": "modify",
      "proposal": "Support storing historical data for a minimum of 4 years while utilizing energy-efficient cloud storage solutions."
    }
